  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "invincible stun combo on the weakest enemy: true damage splash, HP drain, max HP reduction, and heal and Energy block",
    "skill1": "Passive: battle-start line true damage; wounded cursed enemies spawn summons. Active: stun, then steal max HP and Energy",
    "skill2": "single-target multi-hit, then AoE damage with stacking Vitality reduction",
    "skill3": "battle DEF penetration increase, higher while summons are on the battlefield",
    "skill4": "opening true damage crits and cuts max HP; summons steal ATK for themselves and the caster; battle-start summon",
    "skill5": "on defeat, possesses a summon with damage reduction and lower enemy focus"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Baden]] opens each fight by cursing the enemy line in front of him with **true damage**. Every cursed enemy that drops below half HP spawns an **invincible phantom** that fights beside him. His ultimate locks the weakest enemy in a **stunned combo** that ends with true damage, an HP drain, and a **heal and Energy block**. His skills steal max HP, Energy, and ATK, so he grows stronger while phantoms stay on the field. When he falls with a phantom alive, he **possesses it** and keeps fighting with less damage taken. He wants a full enemy line in front of him at battle start to spread the curse. He struggles when he is **burst before phantoms appear**.",
  "counter_overview": "In PVP, [[Baden]] is decided in the opening seconds: if he survives until phantoms appear, he becomes very hard to finish. His curse only covers that one line, so keep your carries out of the lane facing him and kill him before cursed units fall low enough to spawn phantoms. His early ultimate locks your weakest unit in a stun combo while he is **invincible**, then blocks its healing and Energy, so cancel it with [[Lily May]] and hold burst until the combo ends. He has few defensive tools outside that cast, and both his DEFs are high, so delete him with true-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Zorya]]. If he falls with a phantom alive he **possesses it** and enemies stop prioritizing him for a few seconds, so keep lasting wide ultimates like [[Shemira]] or [[Frieren]] running."
}